extra = [('Lagged outcome, spillover and concordant dating', [
    "Three designs were added. (i) Lagged outcome: the 2021–2025 total effect was re-estimated with the 1985–1989 heat island and back-cast impervious cover as additional confounders, in cells with back-cast impervious cover below 5% in 1985–1989 and in all cells, and compared with the main adjustment set on the same cells. (ii) Spillover: own-cell impervious cover and its 1-km (9 × 9 cells) neighbourhood mean were residualized on the confounders and entered jointly, giving own and neighbourhood effects per ten percentage points. (iii) Concordant dating: treated cells were converted according to both the back-cast (increase of at least ten percentage points) and ESA CCI (increase of the urban fraction of at least 0.2) within the same interval; controls were unconverted in both (back-cast increase below five points, CCI increase below 0.05). Pre-period, conversion and post-period changes of heat-island intensity were regressed on the back-cast dose with DML. Net effects subtract the pre-period coefficient (parallel trends relative to the last pre-period) or, with two pre-periods, extrapolate a linear pre-trend[@rambachan2023]. We also report the inner half of each radius and the main estimate without the eleven purposively included or replaced cities."]),
 ('Decision metrics and further checks', [
    "For screening, cities were sorted into thirds by their own total effect and by each model's continent-out answer; we report the share placed in the same third (95% bootstrap interval over cities), the recall of the top third and the share misplaced by two thirds. A nonlinear causal transfer model fitted the pseudo-outcome Ỹ/D̃ with weights D̃² by LightGBM (R-learner[@nie2021]). The within-city change of the effect with climate was estimated by regressing the epoch cross-sections on epoch warm-season maximum temperature with city fixed effects and inverse-variance weights (city bootstrap). Overpass time is the median local solar time of the scenes used; the influence of scene number was estimated in the same fixed-effects regression. The calibration slope regresses WorldCover impervious cover on the out-of-fold back-cast in 2021–2025."])]
